  "question": {
    "text": "The solutions of $(x+y+1) d y=d x$ are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PnbVe",
      "text": "$x+y+2=C e^{y}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "gEYUf",
      "text": "$x+y+4=C \\log y$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kHLLq",
      "text": "$\\quad \\log (x+y+2)=C y$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OrJ21",
      "text": "$\\log (x+y+2)=C-y$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Putting $x+y+1=u,$ we have $d u=d x+d y$ and the given equation reduces to $u(d u-d x)=$ $d x$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{u d u}{u+1}=d x \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad u-\\log (u+1)=x$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\log (x+y+2)=y+$ constant\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow x+y+2=C e^{y}$",
    "image": null
  },
